Use `\addplot table` and tell PGFPlots to use the *row index* as the x‑coordinate. If your file `data` contains one y value per line, this is the simplest:

```latex
\documentclass{standalone}
\usepackage{pgfplots}
\pgfplotsset{compat=1.18}

\begin{document}
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}
  \addplot table[
    y index=0,      % first (and only) column is y
    x expr=\coordindex % x = 0,1,2,... for each line
  ] {data};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{document}
```

- `data` example (no header needed):
  ```
  1.2
  0.8
  1.5
  1.1
  ```

If you want x to start at 1 instead of 0, use:

```latex
x expr=\coordindex+1
```

